1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:10,866
A walk-in order: Dan Kim needs two 15" x 30" shaker doors. Doors are made on the Custom parts page.

2
00:00:10,866 --> 00:00:20,477
Shaker 70 style, in paint-grade MDF.

3
00:00:20,477 --> 00:00:32,172
Size from the old door: 15" wide, 30" high. Two of them.

4
00:00:32,172 --> 00:00:34,529
Hinges on the left, to match the old door, on the Salice cup pattern.

5
00:00:34,529 --> 00:00:40,008
A pull with 128 mm centres, near the top as on a base door.

6
00:00:40,008 --> 00:00:43,903
Add door: it becomes a custom part with its machining already set up.

7
00:00:43,903 --> 00:00:54,573
Open it: panel recess, hinge cups, pull holes and the cut-out are all there.

8
00:00:54,573 --> 00:01:09,403
Now the job: New job, J2066, Kim replacement doors.

9
00:01:09,403 --> 00:01:17,097
No cabinets this time. On the job's Custom parts tab, add the door from the part library.

10
00:01:17,097 --> 00:01:22,102
Nesting places both doors on an MDF sheet, and the rest is kept as an offcut.

11
00:01:22,102 --> 00:01:27,309
Labels: each door gets one, like any cabinet part.

12
00:01:27,309 --> 00:01:32,106
The export check: custom-part machining output is off, so nothing goes to the machine yet.

13
00:01:32,106 --> 00:01:35,308
Simulate in woodWOP before turning that switch on. Two doors, ready to cut once it is.
